        "paragraphs": [
          "Time. A day passes every 1 second. Days begin after 1 Wanaxes join.",
          "Foot soldiers cross a plains hex in 1 day, olive woodland in 1.5, hills or cedar forest in 2, desert in 3. War chariots cross plains in 0.67 day but need 2 in olive woodland and 3 in hills, cedar forest or desert. A full-crewed galley crosses 3 coastal or 5 open-sea hexes a day.",
          "Your Host carries 1200 grain and 480 silver. It lives on subsistence until founding; these reserves do not drain. Find your place \u2014 founding is final.",
          "Food first. A city must feed itself. Starvation makes it shrink; below 50 people it falls.",
          "The gods. A new Wanax starts at 40 Kharis. It fades slowly from the start; each additional city increases the daily cost, even with a temple. A temple takes 16 days to build: staff and feed it to earn favour. Low standing risks punishment.",
